From: System Electronics
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: wait for the VSG to stop at disable

VID_EN is cleared and the function returns right away. The DPI
reprogramming that follows takes the data away while the video stream
generator is still finishing its frame, and the generator then fails
to restart on the next enable.

Measured on 20 instrumented pipeline exits: the 3 that stopped without
ERR_MISSING_DATA all came back, the 17 that did not all failed. A clean
stop takes 2.26 ms and the slowest stop seen, on an exit that was already
losing data, takes 18 ms, so the wait is bounded at 50 ms. The poll
returns as soon as the generator stops, so a wider bound costs nothing on
the exits that do not need it.

The wait runs in the atomic commit tail, which may sleep, so the sleeping
form of readl_poll_timeout is used. cdns_dsi.disable_wait_ms bounds it and
cdns_dsi.vsg_disable_timeouts counts the times it expired.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -696,17 +696,38 @@
 	return MODE_OK;
 }
 
+static unsigned int disable_wait_ms = 50;
+module_param(disable_wait_ms, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(disable_wait_ms, "Max ms to wait at disable for the video stream generator to stop");
+
+static unsigned int vsg_disable_timeouts;
+module_param(vsg_disable_timeouts, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(vsg_disable_timeouts, "Disables where the generator was still running when the wait expired");
+
 static void cdns_dsi_bridge_disable(struct drm_bridge *bridge)
 {
 	struct cdns_dsi_input *input = bridge_to_cdns_dsi_input(bridge);
 	struct cdns_dsi *dsi = input_to_dsi(input);
-	u32 val;
+	u32 val, sts;
+	int ret;
 
 	val = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_DATA_CTL);
 	val &= ~(IF_VID_SELECT_MASK | IF_VID_MODE | VID_EN | HOST_EOT_GEN |
 		 DISP_EOT_GEN);
 	writel(val, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_DATA_CTL);
 
+	/* Let the generator finish before anything reprograms the input. */
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(dsi->regs + VID_MODE_STS, sts,
+				 !(sts & VSG_RUNNING), 100,
+				 disable_wait_ms * 1000);
+	if (ret) {
+		vsg_disable_timeouts++;
+		if (vsg_disable_timeouts == 1 || !(vsg_disable_timeouts % 16))
+			dev_warn(dsi->base.dev,
+				 "video stream generator still running %u ms after VID_EN, VID_MODE_STS 0x%08x (%u so far)\n",
+				 disable_wait_ms, sts, vsg_disable_timeouts);
+	}
+
 	val = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN) & ~IF_EN(input->id);
 	writel(val, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_EN);
 	pm_runtime_put(dsi->base.dev);
